/E (Despite advances in understanding AD pathogenesis, development of effective therapeutics remains challenging. One major limitation is the lack of physiologically relevant preclinical models. Murine models, while widely used, differ significantly from human skin in structure, immune composition, and barrier properties. Similarly, ex vivo human skin explants undergo rapid tissue degradation following excision, limiting their utility for long-term studies and microbiome investigations.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
